    "summary": "Cap tailored from strips of Yoruba aso oke cloth; the strips are all of the same pattern, and made from hand-spun dyed indigo cotton thread, together with imported European thread of white and black cotton. The strips have been hand-woven and hand-sewn together. The warp is made of stripes of the three colours of thread, while the weft uses an indigo ground together with supplementary float bundles of white and black cotton. In larger pieces of the same cloth (seeAf1991,14.6.b and c.), it can be seen that white cotton has been used in some of the weft to give a further patterning to the fabric. The cap is lined with machine-woven blue cotton.",
